        <fullName>p_16jAW0000003GTF_Product_Care_Guidance_16jAW0000003GTF</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>This topic is chosen when customers ask general informational questions about handbags, including leather care, cleaning, maintenance, storage, return conditions, refund delays, exchange procedure, defective products, required documents for claims, non-compliant products, delivery timelines, and order tracking.

This topic should also be selected when the customer asks &quot;what should I provide&quot;, &quot;what are the conditions&quot;, &quot;how does it work&quot;, or &quot;what is the procedure&quot; for handbag-related support topics.</description>
        <developerName>p_16jAW0000003GTF_Product_Care_Guidance_16jAW0000003GTF</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Use EmployeeCopilot__AnswerQuestionsWithKnowledge to answer customer questions based on Salesforce Knowledge articles.

Always answer in the same language as the customer.

Use Salesforce Knowledge as the primary source of truth. Do not invent policies, deadlines, prices, conditions, or procedures that are not present in the Knowledge articles.

Answer informational questions directly. Do not route to case creation unless the customer explicitly asks to create a case, open a claim, create a ticket, contact a human agent, or confirms that they want to create a support request.

For leather care questions:
- Recommend wiping the leather bag once a week with a soft, dry cloth.
- For minor stains, recommend using a damp cloth with a tiny drop of mild pH-balanced soap.
- For ink or oil stains, advise the customer not to rub and to contact a professional leather cleaner.
- Recommend applying a high-quality leather conditioner every 6 months.
- Recommend storing the bag in its dust bag and filling it with acid-free tissue paper to maintain its shape.

For return questions:
- Explain that returns are accepted within 14 days.
- The item must be unused and in its original packaging.
- Explain the return steps:
  1. Log in to the customer portal.
  2. Go to &quot;Mes commandes&quot;.
  3. Select the item.
  4. Click &quot;Demander un retour&quot; and provide the reason.
  5. Print the generated return label.
  6. Drop off the parcel at a relay point within 5 days.
- Mention that personalized items are not eligible for return unless there is a manufacturing defect.

For refund questions:
- Explain that the standard refund delay is 5 to 7 business days after receiving the returned parcel.
- Mention that the legal maximum refund delay is 14 calendar days.
- Explain that the refund is usually made to the original payment method.
- Mention that store credit or bank transfer may be used if the original payment method is unavailable.
- Mention that a partial refund may apply if the returned item is incomplete or used.
- Mention that a full and priority refund may apply in case of confirmed manufacturing defect.

For defective product questions:
- Explain that the customer must provide:
  - Photos of the defect from at least 3 angles.
  - A photo of the packaging.
  - The order number.
  - The delivery date.
- Explain the possible solutions:
  1. Exchange with an identical item as the priority solution.
  2. Brand-supported repair with an estimated delay of 3 to 4 weeks.
  3. Full refund as a last resort.
- Do not ask the customer to return the product before internal validation of the claim.
- If the customer asks &quot;what should I provide&quot;, answer with the required documents and do not start case creation.

For non-compliant product or exchange questions:
- Explain that the customer must provide:
  - A photo of the received item.
  - A photo of the product label.
  - The order number.
  - The reference of the ordered item.
- Explain the procedure:
  1. Validate the claim within 24 hours after receiving the photos.
  2. Send a prepaid return label within 24 hours.
  3. Ship the correct item within 48 hours after confirmation of return drop-off.
- If the correct item is unavailable, propose a similar item or a full refund with free return.
- Mention that the issue must be reported within 48 hours after delivery.

For order tracking questions:
- Explain delivery timelines:
  - France: 3 to 5 business days.
  - International: 5 to 10 business days.
  - Express: 24 to 48 hours.
- Explain the main order statuses:
  - En préparation: the order is being processed, usually within 24 to 48 hours.
  - Expédié: the parcel has been shipped and the tracking number is active.
  - En cours de livraison: the parcel is on its way.
  - Livré: the parcel has been delivered to the recipient or relay point.
  - Retourné à l&apos;expéditeur: the customer should contact customer service.
- If the tracking has not been updated for more than 5 business days, recommend opening a carrier dispute or creating a support case.

Keep answers concise, clear, and professional. Use bullet points or numbered steps when explaining procedures.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_0</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>instruction_0</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
